1	{
2	 "gdd": "design/gdd/2d-lighting-and-occlusion.md",
3	 "blockers": [
4	  {
5	   "where": "LO-1 (L162), LO-2 cadence list (L166), LO-11 wall-change rule (L223), Edge Cases (L908-910), AC-LO-1/-15 (L1318, L1339) versus ADR-0009 § 1, § 3 (stage 0 PROJECT; PROJECTOR table; L151, L215)",
6	   "issue": "The sync replaced 'render callback' with 'LIGHTING present step' everywhere, including the occluder builder. ADR-0009 puts Lighting's occluder builder in a separate PROJECTOR registrant at stage 0 (PROJECT), registered after the layout projector and body.projector. It is the only class allowed to create LightOccluder2D, and PROJECTOR rebuilds are chunked. The GDD now says that polygons are 'rebuilt and written in the same LIGHTING present step, in one apply step' and that 'all writes occur in the LIGHTING present step'. That contradicts ADR-0009 on where the builder runs (stage 0, not stage 6) and on whether the in-reach rebuild is atomic or chunked. An implementer would put the builder inside the stage-6 PRESENTATION presenter, which has no instantiate/free rights. LO-1 also still says the PROJECTOR class is 'provisional pending a technical-director ruling' with an '-> ADR candidate: occluder projector class'. ADR-0009 settles this, and L1038 still lists the candidate as open. LO-1/LO-2 also say Lighting has 'no after: entry', which now collides with the ADR-0009 PresenterDescriptor `after` field. The occluder builder needs the layout projector to run first.",
7	   "fix": "Split the wording. Say the occluder builder runs in the PROJECT stage (stage 0, ADR-0009 § 1/§ 3), before LIGHTING in the same frame, and the light apply runs in the LIGHTING present step. Restate the 'no half-written set' guarantee as 'the whole in-reach rebuild completes in the stage-0 run, which precedes any LIGHTING present of that frame', and state that it is exempt from or exceeds PROJECTOR chunking for in-reach sections (or ask ADR-0009 to say so). Reword AC-LO-1 and AC-LO-15 to name PROJECT and LIGHTING separately. Update LO-1 and L1038 to mark the PROJECTOR-class candidate as closed by ADR-0009 § 1. Clarify that 'no `after:` entry' means no kernel hook order, not the presenter `after` field."
8	  },
9	  {
10	   "where": "Sources and ADR candidates list (L1038)",
11	   "issue": "The amendment marks the 'Renderer and driver (Forward+ versus Compatibility; the explicit driver is closed by ADR-0009 § 3)' candidate as closed by the wrong ADR. ADR-0009 § 3 is the PresentationDriver and stage order. The rendering driver is ADR-0008 § 1, which is provisional and gated by spike steps 1, 2 and 9. The same sync correctly cites ADR-0008 § 1 at L29, L39 and L1018. A reader following this pointer finds nothing about Vulkan, and the candidate looks closed when ADR-0008 says it is provisional.",
12	   "fix": "Change it to 'the explicit driver is pinned provisionally to Vulkan by ADR-0008 § 1, reversible at spike steps 1, 2 and 9'."
13	  }
14	 ]
15	}

